    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 11 with a concentrated offensive profile, anchored by the high-upside pairing of **Junior Caminero** (65.38) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92). **Junior Caminero** projects as our premier play against Gausman, buoyed by a favorable batting order placement and a solid park factor that offsets the veteran pitcher's skill. Meanwhile, **Casey Schmitt** represents our most efficient value play; his score is significantly elevated by a +19% SP skill boost stemming from the exploitable 5.30 xERA of Sasaki. While **Yordan Alvarez** (60.94) remains a lineup staple despite a tougher assignment against Kirby, his elite 0.429 xwOBA ensures he remains a high-floor selection regardless of the matchup difficulty.\n\nManaging the fringes of the roster remains the primary challenge in this 5x5 format, particularly as we monitor the scarcity of stolen bases. **Luke Raley** (52.77) secured the final OF slot primarily due to a positive platoon edge against Lambert, narrowly edging out depth options. We are currently navigating a quiet day for our high-speed assets; **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Christian Yelich** are all unavailable today due to schedule gaps or injury, limiting our ability to attack the SB category. With **Hyeseong Kim** (40.48) occupying the shortstop position, we are forced to accept a significant SP skill penalty against the 2.60 xERA of McDonald, but his inclusion is mandatory to maintain lineup coverage. No significant weather concerns are flagged for today, though owners should monitor the lineup status for **Kazuma Okamoto** (49.31) to ensure the 4-hole projection holds, as any drop in order would likely push him below our 40-point efficiency threshold.",
